{
  "note": "Integer rupees everywhere -- no floats, no toFixed. price <= mrp. The discount percentage is DERIVED, never stored. `new`, `sale`, `low-stock` and `sold-out` are DERIVED too: `badges` holds only what a human chose. Variants carry `delta`, never a price, and ONLY THE SIZE AXIS may carry a non-zero one -- for a garment that is real: XL and XXL take more cloth. `swatch` is a literal hex and is the one permitted literal colour in this project -- it is product data, not theme, taken from a plain patch of cloth in that colour's own photograph, and tokens.pl never sees it because tokens.pl reads only styles/*.css. `sizeChart` names a chart in shop.json; data.pl fails if the chart is missing or does not cover every size this product sells. `skus` is the STOCK OF EACH COLOUR IN EACH SIZE, keyed colour/size (a product with only one axis keys by that axis alone, and one with neither by `one`); a product's `stock` is their sum, worked out when the catalogue loads (domain.js withStock) and never stored, so the two cannot disagree. THE PHOTOGRAPHS ARE THE OWNER'S OWN (8 November 2026), under img/products/. THE PRICES AND THE STOCK ARE NOT REAL YET -- the owner: \"right now you can keep random prices\". SINCE 8 NOVEMBER 2026 THE DATABASE IS WHERE PRODUCTS LIVE: tools/seed.pl writes this file into db/schema.sql, which puts it into an EMPTY products table once; after that the store page adds products and changes prices and stock, and this file is what a page shows only when the database cannot be reached, and in the single-file build.",
